WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.600 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Let's make camp at the stone shelter across the water.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.000 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Get some food, tools and a way across first. You plan it.

3
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.600 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: First, harvest the ripe carrots. They restore hunger, and we keep some to replant.

4
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.100 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Can't we just get going? Why look for food first?

5
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.900 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Hunger is at 8. There's food right here, so let's stock up and have some on the way.

6
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.300 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Eat one of the carrots you just picked, and keep the rest.

7
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.700 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Ate one fresh carrot. Keeping the other one.

8
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.700 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: I'll walk to the edge of the slope and take a look. You do the rest.

9
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: OK, you go. I'm keeping track of the goal and the materials.

10
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.800 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: The crafting table is right here. A wooden pickaxe for mining stone, or a wooden sword for defense?

11
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.000 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Which do you think is more useful?

12
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.100 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: The pickaxe. We can't mine the stone in front of us without a tool, and we need it to get cobblestone.

13
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.500 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: OK. Make the one you said.

14
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.300 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: OK, doing that.

15
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.900 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: The tool is ready. Now let's work out how to cross the water.

16
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.600 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Wait, don't pave the path with the planks. I want to keep four to fix the shelter.

17
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.800 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: And no more chopping trees.

18
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Got it. The materials stay as you asked. Next, let's pick a new route.

19
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.700 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: The planks are for the shelter.

20
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:17.700 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Should we follow the edge of the slope, or dig more dirt to pave a way across? You choose.

21
00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.800 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Let's dig some more dirt here and save up enough to pave a path.

22
00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.700 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Then take the slope path. Clear the stone in the way.

23
00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Keep the stone you mine for a weapon.

24
00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:53.800 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Mining the stone blocking the way first. The cobblestone it drops is saved for a weapon.

25
00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.100 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: The way is clear. I stopped once there was room to walk.

26
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.600 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Then make a stone sword.

27
00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.800 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Crafting a stone sword from cobblestone and sticks. We have enough.

28
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.600 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: The tool is ready. Now let's see how to cross the water.

29
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.400 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: We have food and tools now.

30
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.800 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Take the slope path we scouted to the stone shelter with the red eaves across the water.

31
00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:42.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: First I'll follow the scouted path to the rock on the far side, and look for the shelter with the red eaves.

32
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.500 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: I'll do this short stretch.

33
00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.500 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: OK, you go. I'm keeping track of the goal and the materials.

34
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.500 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: OK, your turn again.

35
00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.100 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: OK, picking up where I left off. The materials we agreed on are still set aside.

36
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: We've made it this far. Let me check the way ahead.

37
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.500 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: The roof here is missing a few blocks. Are the planks we kept enough?

38
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:41.700 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: There are four gaps in the roof and seven planks in the bag. Enough, and the ones we kept come in handy.

39
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.900 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Use the four planks we set aside to fill these four gaps in the roof.

40
00:04:54.500 --> 00:05:00.300 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Filling the roof gaps with four oak planks, exactly what we kept for the repair.

41
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Those gaps are filled. The roof is fixed.

42
00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.900 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: What's left in the bag now, and what's it good for?

43
00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:25.000 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: Three oak planks for more repairs, one carrot to eat, the wooden pickaxe for mining, and the stone sword for defense.

44
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:31.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
User: Great. This is our base. I'll take it from here.

45
00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.200 line:0 position:50% size:84% align:center
Jarvis: OK, it's yours. Goal and materials all noted.
